# created: 2026-11-27 | branch: feat/v60-l0-wp01-ownership-map
# author: Larry Klosowski (L0 lane, L0-WP01; Claude Opus 5.5)
# status: active
#
# 0.6.0 lane ownership map (planset 2026-11-07-v060, lanes/L0_INTEGRATION_SEAMS.md section 2 and
# each lane file's "File ownership" section). One source for two consumers:
#   scripts/cx-ownership-check.sh --map v60 <lane> [base]   (lane-guard.yml, every PR + merge group)
#   scripts/gen-codeowners.mjs                              (writes .github/CODEOWNERS)
#
# Row format:  <lanes> <glob>     lanes: l0..l9, lq, frozen, or a comma list (shared file), or '*'
#   - The LAST matching row owns a file (CODEOWNERS rules). Broad rows first, narrow rows later.
#   - '*' matches inside one path segment, '**' only as a whole glob or a trailing '/**'.
#   - '*' rows are process files any lane may touch; they never change a file's owner.
#   - 'frozen' paths belong to no lane: no feat/v60-* branch may change them (L0 section 2.3).
#   - 'create:<lanes> <glob>' rows are seed grants, never owners: those lanes may ADD a matching file
#     that does not exist at the base. Editing or deleting it afterwards is its owner's alone.
#     CODEOWNERS ignores them (review still routes to the owner's reviewers).
#   - A glob never ends in '/' (CODEOWNERS would read a directory, the matcher a literal path).
#   - A lane that needs a file it does not own asks through an L0 seam PR; only L0 edits this map.
# Partial-file ownership in the lane files (line ranges, "only the X area") is recorded as whole-file
# ownership plus a comment; the lane keeps to its part in review.
#
# CODEOWNERS directives. Reviewers come from the federation repos/citrate-core/owners.md (code
# review: Saul plus one, the maintainers team). 'tail' rules are written last so they always win:
# the CL-S4 sign-off record, its packet copy and the signer registry need the owner's approval
# (V60 MESH-2; GitHub accepts any one listed owner, so the security lead's part is their signature
# in the record, which the build verifies against signers.json).
#! reviewers * @CitrateNetwork/maintainers
# LQ-WP03 (#789, seam L0-WP01a): the tripwire registry, its rule, its check, the check's own tests and
# the workflow decide whether a registered tripwire may go (only for a stricter replacement), so the
# owner approves every change to them. The lane rows below still name LQ as the lane that edits them.
#! tail /.agentile/coverage/tripwires.json @SaulBuilds
#! tail /.agentile/coverage/TRIPWIRES.md @SaulBuilds
#! tail /scripts/ci/lq/tripwire-inventory.mjs @SaulBuilds
#! tail /scripts/ci/lq/tripwire-inventory.test.mjs @SaulBuilds
#! tail /.github/workflows/lq-tripwires.yml @SaulBuilds
#! tail /release/signoffs/ @SaulBuilds

